<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Armenians</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Armenian</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Armenians are a people of the Armenian highlands with their own language and Christian church. Armenian merchants played major roles in long-distance trade, especially in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/safavid-empire">Safavid Empire</a>, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbas-i-of-persia">Abbas I</a> resettled them at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-julfa">New Julfa</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isfahan">Isfahan</a>. Armenians also served as soldiers and officials in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimid Caliphate</a>, and in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> they were a major community until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genocide">genocide</a> of 1915.</p></div>
